            "It begins as a small kink in the boundary between cold polar air and warm tropical air, the **polar front**. If the upper-level winds are favourable, the kink grows into a wave. The cold air pushes south and the warm air pushes north, and the whole thing starts to turn around a centre of low pressure, like a whirlpool in a stream.",
